  "notes": "The congregation records the 1839 nave, the 1861 wings, the 1895 brick tower, and a 2.5 m roof raise in 1928. Morne’s exact 2007 public-domain Qualla image establishes the cream stucco, red-brown roof, triple openings, clock, lunette and curved gable shoulders."
